# #855 (a #850 follow-up, 2026-09-19) -- Cloudflare Workers' own default
# for every static asset is `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0,
# must-revalidate` (confirmed against https://developers.cloudflare.com/
# workers/static-assets/headers/, not assumed), which forces a real
# network round-trip for every asset on every load -- a fast 304 on a
# hit, but still a full round-trip's worth of latency, paid again and
# again. Measured directly (real GPRS-equivalent throttling, Playwright's
# CDP Network.emulateNetworkConditions, against the real production
# build): a normal reload with a warm cache took ~12.5s -- indistinguishable
# from having the browser's HTTP cache disabled entirely -- proof that
# must-revalidate's round-trip, not bandwidth, is the actual cost here.
# ~9.4s (a real ~25% improvement) with this file in place.
#
# vite.deploy.config.js's own entryFileNames/chunkFileNames give every
# chunk under /-/chunks/ a content hash in its filename -- any
# code change produces a new URL, so a cached copy of the OLD URL can
# never go stale; safe to cache "forever" (no revalidation at all, not
# even a fast one).
/-/chunks/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable

# #857 -- the top-level *-app.js/tailwind.css/components/*.js files have
# stable, un-hashed names (views/*.njk reference them by a fixed path),
# so a bare immutable rule on the path alone would mean a real deploy
# silently never reaching an already-visited browser. .eleventy.js's own
# assetVersion global (a single value per real `eleventy` invocation)
# is appended as ?v=... to every reference to these files instead
# (views/_includes/app-layout.njk and the five standalone pages that
# don't go through it -- login/register/reset-password/index/help) --
# the query string becomes part of the browser's own cache key, so a
# real rebuild's new value is a guaranteed cache MISS (fetched fresh),
# while every future request to that exact versioned URL is a hit,
# forever. Skipped entirely for dev builds (isDevBuild) -- see that
# template's own comment on why an unversioned request still needs to
# reach vite.config.js's own devEntryRewrite middleware unchanged.
#
# service-worker.js (#983, was sw.js) is NOT listed here, deliberately: it's the service worker
# script itself, which browsers already special-case for update
# checking (a new registration is compared byte-for-byte against the
# previous one on its own schedule, independent of HTTP caching) --
# immutable caching on its URL would fight that mechanism, not help it.
#
# Explicit filenames, not a single /-/*-app.js pattern -- the
# _headers glob syntax's one documented example only shows a trailing
# `/*`, so a mid-segment wildcard's support is unconfirmed; listing
# vite.entries.mjs's own CLIENT_ENTRIES keys (as "<key>-app.js") is
# unambiguous. Add a line here whenever a new entry is added there --
# the same "one list, not two copies that silently drift" lesson that
# file's own comment already states, extended to this file too.
/-/tailwind.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable
/-/components/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable
